Builds on patch 1 (46beb5d).

Approval endpoints (src/features/auth/):
- GET  /api/v1/auth/pending-approvals — org_admin sees all pending
  requests in the org; manager sees only requests for teams they
  manage. Optional ?teamId= filter.
- POST /api/v1/auth/pending-approvals/:userId/approve — eligible
  approver is the named requestedManagerId, any manager of the
  requested team, or any org_admin. Transactional: flips user.status
  to 'active' AND inserts the user_team_role row in one DB transaction.
- POST /api/v1/auth/pending-approvals/:userId/reject — same
  eligibility, accepts an optional reason.

Route protection: requireAuth now guards every internal feature
router (candidates, clients, teams, job-postings, applications,
performance, credits, workflow, organizations read/update) which
were previously wide open behind a forgeable x-tenant-id header.
requirePermission(entity, action) is layered on top wherever seed.ts
has an unambiguous matching permission key; requireModule() added
where a plan module clearly gates the feature.

Also fixes a tenant/auth ordering bug: the global tenant middleware
ran before route-level requireAuth and was rejecting requests that
had a valid Bearer token but no x-tenant-id header. tenant.js now
defers to requireAuth whenever a Bearer token is present.

Several routes intentionally left behind requireAuth only (no
requirePermission) where the seed data doesn't cleanly support one —
each flagged with an inline NOTE and documented in walkthrough.md
'Known Gaps' rather than guessing at permission semantics
(candidates:delete, job_postings:delete/close, applications base
CRUD, workflow template CRUD, strategy, credits top-up/adjust,
organizations platform-admin scoping).

walkthrough.md rewritten to reflect current architecture (16 schema
modules, real Postgres/Drizzle) and document both auth patches plus
the known gaps and next steps.

Tests: 18/18 passing (added auth-required negative tests + signed-JWT
positive tests for previously-open routes; existing tests updated
from x-tenant-id-only to Bearer auth).
